   "phrasing": "greet_01"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Pretty good, thanks for asking.",
   "est_sec": 1.65,
   "gap_before": 0.76,
   "event": "greeting_answer",
   "phrasing": "greet_ans_02"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "My cat keeps scratching the furniture and I'm trying to pick a fix.",
   "est_sec": 4.13,
   "gap_before": 0.54,
   "block": "pets.opt2"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "I'm going to list all the options first, so please don't comment until I'm done.",
   "est_sec": 4.75,
   "gap_before": 0.8,
   "event": "instruction",
   "kind": "describe_options",
   "phrasing": "describe_instr_02"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "No worries.",
   "est_sec": 0.72,
   "gap_before": 0.33,
   "role": "ack",
   "phrasing": "ack_14"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "One option is a really tall scratching post right next to the couch.",
   "est_sec": 4.13,
   "gap_before": 0.88,
   "block": "pets.opt2",
   "event": "distractor",
   "kind": "pause"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Another is putting sticky tape on the arms of the sofa so she hates touching it.",
   "est_sec": 5.06,
   "gap_before": 2.02,
   "block": "pets.opt2",
   "event": "distractor",
   "kind": "pause"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Or I could get those soft caps that go over her claws, which last about a month.",
   "est_sec": 5.37,
   "gap_before": 1.81,
   "block": "pets.opt2"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "And that's the last one. What do you think?",
   "est_sec": 2.89,
   "gap_before": 1.43,
   "event": "return_cue",
   "kind": "explicit",
   "phrasing": "describe_cue_11"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Have you tried a scratching post before? If not, I'd start with the tall post plus the tape for a few weeks. If she ignores the post completely, the claw caps are a good backup.",
   "est_sec": 10.95,
